<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Unit 2 Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00351</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Unit 2 Overview: Why should I care?</md:title>
    <md:uuid>36195c69-e0b8-489e-ab45-c693c36ef933</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Why should I care?</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Do you ever set goals for yourself? Perhaps you have a goal to make your school’s
        basketball team, or you have a goal to improve your GPA next semester.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Just as you might set goals for yourself, businesses set goals for themselves. These
        goals often relate to producing a quality product, staying on budget, and making a profit
        for the company.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">Watch the video to discover how entrepreneur Nafy Flatley has worked to achieve her goal
        of bringing the food of Senegal to the world, and how she might use linear inequalities to
        create a healthy and affordable product.</para>

      <media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text">
        <iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://openstax.org/r/business-inequalities"/>
      </media>

      <para id="para-00004">In this unit, you will learn about solving systems of linear equations, linear
        inequalities, and systems of linear inequalities. Understanding how to solve these types of
        equations, inequalities, and systems can help you in your daily life. For example, solving
        systems of linear equations can help you with deciding which of two phone plans with
        different flat fees and different costs per text charges is the better deal based on your
        usage.</para>
        <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Building Character: Growth Mindset</title>
      <para id="para-00005">As an entrepreneur, Nafy Flatley must embrace challenges and try new strategies as she
        works to make her business a success. Similarly, in this course, you may be faced with
        challenges as you work through new skills and concepts. Being able to learn from mistakes
        and struggles is an important skill to have both in and out of the classroom.</para>
      <para id="para-00006">Throughout this unit, you will work on developing a growth mindset. Having a growth
        mindset means believing you can improve your abilities. Compared to a fixed mindset, a
        growth mindset encourages you to embrace challenges, sustain effort, and try new strategies.
        Of course, no one embodies only a growth or fixed mindset; we are all a mixture of the two,
        and we can learn to recognize what triggers a fixed versus growth mindset. The brain is like
        a muscle—something you can strengthen.</para>
      <para id="para-00007">Think about your current sense of having a growth mindset. How many of the following
        statements are true for you?</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>After I make a mistake, I always look for ways to learn from it.</item>
        <item>I love challenges because they make me smarter.</item>
        <item>I truly believe that people can change.</item>
        <item>I can always change how intelligent I am.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00008">Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes
        time. Your first step starts today!</para>
    </section>
    </section>

    <section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Am I ready to learn this?</title>

    <section id="sect-00004">
      <title>Getting Ready for Unit 2</title>
      <para id="para-00009">To be ready for this unit, you need to be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>Determine if an ordered pair is a solution to a linear equation.</item>
        <item>Work with slope-intercept form of a linear equation.</item>
        <item>Find the <m:math><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:math>- and <m:math><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:math>-intercepts of a line when
          given its equation.</item>
      </list>

      <para id="para-00010">Next, you will answer some questions that will help you see how ready you are for this
        unit. If you need help, some mini-lessons will help you brush up on anything you need to
        work on.</para>
    </section>
    </section>
